lio: rust snippet idea (very short):
```rust
// redwood-rs: try proxy KMS, fallback to cached token
use std::fs;
use reqwest::blocking::Client;
fn main(){
  let client = Client::builder().timeout(std::time::Duration::from_secs(2)).build().unwrap();
  let res = client.get("https://kms.private.example/token").send();
  let token = match res {
    Ok(r) => r.text().unwrap_or_default(),
    Err(_) => fs::read_to_string("/var/lib/redwood/kms.token.cache").unwrap_or_default(),
  };
  println!("token: {}", token);
}
```
rafa: systemd reload snippet:
```bash
sudo cp /tmp/new-proxy.crt /etc/redwood/proxy.crt
sudo systemctl reload redwood-proxy.service
# verify pinned fingerprint
openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256 -in /etc/redwood/proxy.crt
```
tess: troubleshooting bullets: "proxy cert rejected by clients" -> check CA chain, check pinned fingerprint on hosts, ensure control-plane accepted cert. "bastion POST fails" -> verify allowed IP, check control-plane ACLs, check time sync.
zara: added a tiny CLI to update fingerprint on hosts: `redwoodctl cert pin --fingerprint SHA256:AB:... --hosts @private-nodes` and note that this runs via the private control plane agent. marked as admin-only.
